Use io and string.

Define function count_and_say taking n as a whole number returning TcString:
    Let current be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("1"), bytes_len("1")).
    Let step start at 1.
    Repeat while step < n:
        Let buffer be block of 1024 byte.
        Let written start at 0 as an unsigned number.
        Let i start at 0 as an unsigned number.
        Let current length be length of address of current.
        Repeat while i is less than current length:
            Let run start at 1 as an unsigned number.
            Repeat while i + run is less than current length:
                Let prior be current.data[i].
                Let following be current.data[i + run].
                If prior isn't equal to following:
                    Break.
                Add 1 to run.
            If run is at least 10:
                Set item written of buffer to 48 + (run divided by 10) as a byte.
                Add 1 to written.
            Set item written of buffer to 48 + (run modulo 10) as a byte.
            Add 1 to written.
            Set item written of buffer to current.data[i].
            Add 1 to written.
            Add run to i.
        Let next be create text from address of item 0 of buffer of length written.
        str_free(address of current).
        Set current to next.
        Add 1 to step.
    Give back current.
Done.

Let first be count_and_say(1).
Let fourth be count_and_say(4).
Let fifth be count_and_say(5).
Say first.
Say fourth.
Say fifth.
str_free(address of fifth).
str_free(address of fourth).
str_free(address of first).
Return 0.
